reated_at":"2025-03-10T09:45:00Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T14:12:32Z","closed_at":"2026-08-31T14:12:32Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- reproducible in 4.4-stable\n- not reproducible in 4.3-stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.3.1) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Mobile) - integrated Apple M3 Max (Apple9) - Apple M3 Max (14 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nAutomatic UI navigation has seemingly regressed updating my project from 4.3 to 4.4 and I managed to make at least one MRP highlighting the issue. In the small video of the MRP below, I'm pressing ui_down and expect the focus to move to the button label below it, but instead it moves to the left.\n\nIt seems to have to do specifically with the left button being taller than the right button. That shouldn't matter for UI navigation, as the right bottom button is still clearly the best candidate when pressing ui_down from the up right button.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0c2a3f37-66bf-48e2-8ba6-3db9a8ea149a\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open and run the MRP.\n2. Press down.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[focus-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19159691/focus-mrp.zip)\n\n### EDIT: Proposed improvements\n\nThis is an issue report but the discussion on this page on how to improve this functionality has been great - skip to @rsubtil to see some methods of how automatic navigation can be improved: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103895#issuecomment-4019746235","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api